            "Visual_Notice_AvgOfAvg": "This is an average of averages. Power BI averaged the field at the grain of every bound dimension, and those averages are combined here, so each combination counts the same whether it holds one row or ten thousand. The weights are not in the data the visual receives, so it cannot correct for them. Bind only the dimensions you compare, or use a measure that carries its own weighting.",
            "Visual_Notice_NonAdditive": "This measure is being collapsed in the visual: Power BI aggregated it at the grain of every bound dimension, and the rest is combined here. If the measure is not additive \u2014 a distinct count, a ratio, a percentage \u2014 the number may not be the one you expect. Bind only the dimensions you compare, or use an additive measure.",
